# Force Linux line endings (LF) for all text files, in git storage and on disk.
# Prevents phantom "modified" files when the Linux dev container (LF) and the
# Windows host (CRLF) interpret line endings differently. Everything here runs
# in containers, so LF is the correct convention. Travels with the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run on the Linux droplet — force LF so shebangs don't break
# (a CRLF shebang makes /usr/bin/env look for `bash\r`, which fails).
*.sh text eol=lf